 "help": "usage: wgsextract cohort summarize [-h] [--region REGION] [--bed BED] [--min-depth MIN_DEPTH]\n                                   [--min-gq MIN_GQ] [--format {tsv,parquet}]\n                                   [--include-identifiers]\n                                   MANIFEST\n\npositional arguments:\n  MANIFEST              Local cohort input manifest (wgsextract.cohort/1).\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --region REGION       Limit to an autosomal contig, interval or comma-separated list.\n  --bed BED             Limit to autosomal intervals from a local BED.\n  --min-depth MIN_DEPTH\n                        Minimum DP (block MIN_DP).\n  --min-gq MIN_GQ       Minimum GQ for callers that provide it.\n  --format {tsv,parquet}\n                        Table format: tsv or parquet (needs pyarrow).\n  --include-identifiers\n                        Also write a private participant/QC join with source paths and names.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract cohort summarize cohort.json --region chr22 --outdir summary\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  cohort.variants.tsv (or .parquet) and a result manifest; a private\n  participant join only with --include-identifiers.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools; minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
